---
source: crates/modde-cli/tests/cli_help_snapshots.rs
expression: "stdout(&[\"game\", \"--help\"])"
---
Manage user-defined games

Usage: modde game [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add             Add or overwrite a user-defined game registration
  list            List user-defined games
  remove          Remove a user-defined game registration
  detect          Detect executable-bearing directories under a game install
  show            Show a resolved game registration
  export          Export a game registration to TOML
  import          Import a game registration from TOML
  import-profile  Import OptiScaler profiles from TOML for a game
  help            Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --data-dir <DATA_DIR>          Override data directory (default: ~/.local/share/modde or $`MODDE_DATA_DIR`) [env: MODDE_DATA_DIR=]
      --config-dir <CONFIG_DIR>      Override the base configuration directory used by modde and its session journal
      --heap-profile <HEAP_PROFILE>  Write a DHAT heap profile. Requires the `heap-profile` cargo feature [env: MODDE_HEAP_PROFILE=]
  -h, --help                         Print help
